From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:19:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 374/394] drm/msm/dsi: restore SM8750 bonded slave clock state

The SM8750 slave PHY selects the external bit clock, but still has its own
pixel divider and clock mux. A PHY reset clears those registers. Saving and
restoring only the clock master leaves the slave's hardware state different
from the common clock framework's cached rates.

On Piano at 120 Hz, post-clock register capture shows CMN_CLK_CFG0=0x51
on both PHYs at first boot. After DPMS off/on the master stays at 0x51,
but the slave becomes 0xf1 and immediately reports VID_MDP FIFO overflow.
Its local PLL DECIMAL_DIV_START_1 also changes from 0x1f to 0x41.

Opt SM8750 into saving and restoring the slave's existing PLL/divider
state through the same lifecycle as the master. Keep other PHY variants'
restore policy unchanged. No divider value or display mode is hardcoded.

Piano register capture confirms both dividers return to 0x51 after DPMS
off/on. The previous FIFO fault no longer occurs during the 120 Hz
off/on cycle or 60/120/90/144/120 Hz modeset sequence.

Imported from SunUEFI a485cc01c639: patches/linux/7.2.9/0025-dsi-sm8750-restore-bonded-slave.patch

The manager hunk uses the equivalent piano21 shutdown-order comment as context; all added code and the original semantics are retained.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

[ from github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8750-piano, change c6a971f9bedb
  (13 Oct 2026); the source carries no Signed-off-by ]
[mzak: adapted to the iceland queue as a Kaanapali opt-in: the flag is
 set in dsi_phy_3nm_kaanapali_cfgs only (SM8750 is not changed here, we
 cannot test it). The slave is saved through a new
 msm_dsi_phy_slave_pll_save_state() (no-op unless the PHY is a slave of
 an opted-in config) and restored only after such a save
 (slave_state_saved), so the bootloader state saved at PLL init is not
 written back at the first enable. msm.dsi_slave_pll_restore (default
 off, read at the save) turns it on at runtime for an A/B. Our
 post_disable has no piano21 shutdown-order comment; the save follows
 the master's. Ship only if the read-only register probe shows the
 slave's CMN_CLK_CFG0 / DECIMAL_DIV_START_1 changing over a modeset or
 DPMS cycle on the OnePlus Pad 4]
[mzak: off by default for the q89v trial, to be compared at run time:
 the read-only probe on q89u read the bonded slave's CMN_CLK_CFG0 as
 0xf1 (the master's 0x31) and its DECIMAL_DIV_START_1 as 65 (master
 35), the same over 120 / 60 Hz changes and DPMS]
[ upstream author: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>; picked for the iceland kernel q89v (candidate) ]
